From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: veildawn <40253459+veildawn@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 17:43:49 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Online play settings: relay server, player name and room
 password in the game launchers

The LDN relay client reads only DM_LDNR* environment variables, which a
player cannot set on iPhone and should not have to set on Mac. The iOS
launcher and the Mac settings window gain an Online play section
(docs/LDN-SETTINGS.md): a toggle per game, saved servers with live
address validation, a connection test (HELLO, HELLO_ACK, one PING timed),
the player name within the 32-byte native field, an optional room
password with explicit consent for the plaintext transport, and Copy and
Paste invite (an nx2apple-ldn://join link). Play writes the variables the
host already reads, and a variable set by an env file or the launch
environment wins. Off by default: nothing is set and the host is unchanged.

OnlinePlay.swift is Foundation only, so its regression check
(dm/ios/tests/test_online_play.py) runs on macOS and on Linux with a
Swift toolchain, including a fake relay on loopback.

Upstream-Status: pending
Reason: In-app settings for the LDN relay client (fork feature, depends on 0043)
Issue: veildawn/NX2Apple (owner request, in-app online play settings for the LDN relay)

