+## Online play
+
+**Online play** at the bottom of the screen lets local wireless games reach friends over the internet through an LDN relay server. Turn it on, add the server everyone uses (Add server…), test the connection, and send an invite with **Copy invite**. A friend pastes it with **Paste invite**, and the same server and room password are filled in. A room password is optional and unencrypted, so use one only on a trusted network. The settings are off by default, and on the Mac the servers and the password are shared by every game app while each game decides whether it plays online. The whole design, the invite link and the variables the section sets (`DM_LDNR*`, which an `env.txt` still wins over) are in [Online play settings](LDN-SETTINGS.md) and [LDN relay multiplayer](LDN-RELAY.md).
+
 ## TV
 
 Connect a TV or monitor by cable, or start Screen Mirroring to an Apple TV or AirPlay TV. The game fills it in 16:9 at up to 1080p and switches to **Docked**; the iPhone or iPad keeps the controls. Disconnect to bring the game back to the device in its earlier mode. AirPlay adds some delay; a cable has almost none.
